// AnswerWord is WHAT A CREATURE DID when the world rolled the author's answer
// table (design rpg-project#458, "The outcome vocabulary"; extended by
// rpg-project#465, "The creature's table"). One word per table entry, and an
// entry carries exactly one of them — two words in one entry is an authoring
// error the validator refuses, so this is a single value and never a set.
//
// THE ENUM GROWS A VALUE PER SLICE, never ahead of one, AND THIS SLICE BRINGS
// `time`. The table is no longer rolled only when a social verb resolves
// against a creature: it is also rolled whenever the creature HAS TIME — its
// turn in a fight, or a round of the world clock — and HOLD, ATTACK, TOWARD
// and AWAY are what a creature can do with one turn's worth of doing (design
// rpg-project#465 §2). FACT and FLEE remain event words; the four arriving
// here are time words.
